# The site under website/public is deployed to findra-search.netlify.app on every push to
# main, so it has to be in the repository. Netlify serves it straight from there with no
# build step; netlify.toml names it as the publish directory.

# A runtime lock naming a session and a process id. It regenerates, it is different on every
# machine, and committing it would put a dirty file in every future checkout.
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Review renders. Regenerate with --searchshot; they are a conversation, not a record.
/docs/shots/review/
